            <ArticleTitle>Reaction of Silyllithium, α-Keto N-tert-Butanesulfinyl Imidates and Aldehydes for Asymmetric Synthesis of α-Substituted β-(Silyloxy)-α-hydroxy Acid Derivatives.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10748-10755</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.joc.7b02214</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A single-flask reaction of silyllithium, α-keto N-tert-butanesulfinyl imidates and aldehydes has been developed for the diastereoselective synthesis of α,β-dihydroxy acid derivatives. In this reaction, the nucleophilic addition of silyllithium to chiral α-keto imidates followed by silyl migration forms chiral aza-enolates, which react diastereoselectively with aldehydes. Subsequent [1,4]-O → O silyl migration affords α-substituted β-(silyoxy)-α-hydroxy imidates.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
